      "content": "The primary risk factors involve the inherent flammability of the solvents combined with the confined nature of high-density racking. Thermal runaway is a major concern, as improper containment or heat accumulation can cause sudden, rapid temperature increases leading to ignition. Additionally, insufficient ventilation prevents the safe dispersion of flammable vapors, allowing them to build up to explosive concentrations within the storage area. Proper fire suppression systems and robust segregation protocols are critical mitigation measures.",
