      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Hidden risks often relate to system degradation or cumulative stress, such as unseen corrosion within racking supports or failed electrical connections within the solvent handling equipment. Furthermore, subtle chemical incompatibilities between stored solvents or with building materials, which might not be apparent during a routine visual check, can precede a runaway reaction. Aging seals, minor leaks that slowly accumulate vapors, and inadequate monitoring of localized ambient temperatures are also significant, yet often overlooked, hazards.",
